## BLUEPRINT

The advisor's points are all well-grounded and I've already verified #2 against the live code (build_contained_command L385/398: `inv.env` becomes `--setenv=K=V` for the child python, while MEMMAX is read from `std::env::var` and emitted as `-p MemoryMax=`). The advisor confirms the typed-field transport is correct, and clarifies the admission/auto-size split and the conservative-default property. I'm ready to write the blueprint.

The deliverable is the blueprint text itself returned verbatim. Here it is.

